# Update canvases after each development step

The controlling specification requires two different canvases. Do not copy one over the other.

- `targeted-works.canvas.tsx` is the phase register and the reclassified work list. Update phase status here.
- `progress-done.canvas.tsx` is the history: what was implemented, the limitation that remains, and the date. Do not delete rows.
- `qs-development.canvas.tsx` is the short overview of phase gates. It is not a third copy.

Paths:

- C:\Users\mrlaptop\.cursor\projects\d-QS-Software\canvases\qs-development.canvas.tsx
- C:\Users\mrlaptop\.cursor\projects\d-QS-Software\canvases\targeted-works.canvas.tsx
- C:\Users\mrlaptop\.cursor\projects\d-QS-Software\canvases\progress-done.canvas.tsx

A prototype test passing does not mark a phase GATE PASSED. A phase becomes GATE PASSED only when its exit criteria pass and the phase gate report says so. Do not remove earlier rows.
